  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Size of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mmultiscripts><mi>Bk</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>97</mn><none></none></mmultiscripts><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ion is less than that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mmultiscripts><mi>Np</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>93</mn><none></none></mmultiscripts><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> due to actinide contraction.</p><p>As we know that in a period from left to right ionic radius decreases and in actinide series it is due to actinide&nbsp;contraction.&nbsp;</p>",
